      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Porterville%2C_California",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Founded in 1864, Porterville grew around a Butterfield Overland Mail station that later became a popular hotel called Porter Station.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Porterville%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Three buildings in Porterville— the First Congregational Church, the US Post Office‑Porterville Main, and the Zalud House Museum— are listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Porterville%2C_California",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The city earned the All‑America City Award in 1994, a rare honor given to communities that demonstrate civic excellence.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ci.porterville.ca.us/visitors/about_porterville.php",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Porterville’s historic museum, open Fridays and Saturdays, showcases artifacts that trace the town’s evolution from a frontier stop to a modern community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.portervillemuseum.com/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Porterville is the hometown of Olympic discus gold medalist Sim Iness, who was born in Oklahoma but grew up and trained in the city.",
